[SPEAKER_01]: Because why?

366
00:29:57,668 --> 00:29:58,388
[SPEAKER_01]: Because you feel.

367
00:30:00,489 --> 00:30:02,889
[SPEAKER_01]: And you discern it through those feelings that are being felt.

368
00:30:06,210 --> 00:30:06,830
[SPEAKER_01]: Yes, that's it.

369
00:30:06,870 --> 00:30:08,111
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why you start the body.

370
00:30:08,471 --> 00:30:10,091
[SPEAKER_01]: Seeing that body currently.

371
00:30:10,371 --> 00:30:13,292
[SPEAKER_01]: Just getting the grip, the notion of the principle.

372
00:30:14,218 --> 00:30:17,320
[SPEAKER_01]: And then you can start... What's beyond this?

373
00:30:17,620 --> 00:30:17,920
[SPEAKER_02]: Sorry?

374
00:30:18,120 --> 00:30:20,421
[SPEAKER_02]: Your mind gets larger and more developed.

375
00:30:20,501 --> 00:30:20,741
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

376
00:30:21,301 --> 00:30:28,445
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, it becomes more discerning of the principle, which means... and that... it's a universal principle that is present in everything that is arising.

377
00:30:28,645 --> 00:30:30,026
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why it's a universal principle.

378
00:30:30,706 --> 00:30:33,107
[SPEAKER_01]: Hence, then, you don't have to keep repeating.

379
00:30:33,127 --> 00:30:35,508
[SPEAKER_01]: You just start seeing it, because, yeah, it's arising.

380
00:30:35,528 --> 00:30:38,490
[SPEAKER_01]: Thus, it's partaking to this nature of the same principle that you have understood.

381
00:30:45,977 --> 00:30:51,882
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, and even now, like, there was never, like, a special contemplation between feeling and the contemplation of nutrient.

382
00:30:51,922 --> 00:30:54,163
[SPEAKER_01]: And I think I might have read that sutra, but I don't even remember it.

383
00:30:55,064 --> 00:31:00,068
[SPEAKER_01]: But the point is, you look at the principle and you see exactly what's there, and how it has to be.

384
00:31:02,370 --> 00:31:06,593
[SPEAKER_01]: And more skilled people would maybe describe it in even a greater detail, more accurately.

385
00:31:07,334 --> 00:31:09,455
[SPEAKER_01]: But that's irrelevant.

386
00:31:09,535 --> 00:31:12,678
[SPEAKER_01]: What's important is to see the principle, because that's what frees you from suffering.

387
00:31:14,428 --> 00:31:22,916
[SPEAKER_01]: Fully developing that is how you become an arahant.

388
00:31:26,120 --> 00:31:33,147
[SPEAKER_02]: With the origination of name-form, there is the origination of mind, the cessation of name-form, there is the passing away of mind.

389
00:31:34,047 --> 00:31:36,990
[SPEAKER_01]: So, now that's getting you modifying.

390
00:31:37,331 --> 00:31:37,571
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

391
00:31:40,681 --> 00:31:46,483
[SPEAKER_01]: But, no matter how refined it gets, it doesn't mean it's getting more intricate or more complex.

392
00:31:46,724 --> 00:31:46,944
[SPEAKER_01]: No.

393
00:31:47,744 --> 00:31:57,408
[SPEAKER_01]: It is becoming more subtle within the same principle or principle that was pertaining to the first thing that you read, and the second thing, and the third thing, and then the fourth thing.

394
00:32:02,470 --> 00:32:05,011
[SPEAKER_01]: So, what is then the next thing that people will regard as mine?

395
00:32:06,160 --> 00:32:15,305
[SPEAKER_01]: You have your body, your feelings, and the next thing would be, oh, my mind, this, this ambiguous presence of this mental energy and whatnot, however you want to call it.

396
00:32:16,026 --> 00:32:17,727
[SPEAKER_01]: That's, that's what...

397
00:32:17,747 --> 00:32:18,687
[SPEAKER_01]: Mind, basically.

398
00:32:18,907 --> 00:32:19,428
[SPEAKER_01]: The mental.

399
00:32:20,648 --> 00:32:22,189
[SPEAKER_01]: It's the, it's the, it's the closest to you.

400
00:32:22,229 --> 00:32:25,351
[SPEAKER_01]: It's closer than, more closer than your feelings, and it's more closer than your body.

401
00:32:27,792 --> 00:32:29,073
[SPEAKER_01]: So, how you disown that?

402
00:32:30,214 --> 00:32:31,735
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, by letting it endure.

403
00:32:32,860 --> 00:32:41,323
[SPEAKER_01]: By seeing it arise and by, through its presence, discerning that upon which the mind has to be standing, which is not you.

404
00:32:42,564 --> 00:32:43,484
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's name and form.

405
00:32:43,544 --> 00:32:44,724
[SPEAKER_01]: That is the all.

406
00:32:45,425 --> 00:32:45,665
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

407
00:32:46,105 --> 00:32:46,585
[SPEAKER_01]: The world.

408
00:32:46,945 --> 00:32:47,165
Everything.

409
00:32:47,565 --> 00:32:49,386
[SPEAKER_01]: Anything that can possibly manifest itself.

410
00:32:52,447 --> 00:32:53,828
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you can say the manifestation.

411
00:32:56,849 --> 00:32:58,149
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's something you cannot prevent.

412
00:32:58,609 --> 00:33:00,270
[SPEAKER_01]: In the same sense, the pressures.

413
00:33:00,730 --> 00:33:03,572
[SPEAKER_01]: It's being exerted because of which you feel it's something you cannot prevent.

414
00:33:04,032 --> 00:33:09,036
[SPEAKER_01]: In the same sense, the body, depending on the nutrients that are nourishing the body somehow, it's something you cannot prevent.

415
00:33:09,696 --> 00:33:14,200
[SPEAKER_01]: You cannot be eating nutrients and providing nutrients and saying, may these nutrients not nourish the body.

416
00:33:14,240 --> 00:33:14,440
[SPEAKER_01]: No.

417
00:33:14,860 --> 00:33:18,463
[SPEAKER_01]: They're nutrients because they nourish, because the body directly stands upon it.

418
00:33:19,964 --> 00:33:23,386
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it's the same principle, just a coarser, coarser form of it.

419
00:33:24,027 --> 00:33:26,108
[SPEAKER_01]: But for the mind, which is subtler, it's again the same.

420
00:33:26,148 --> 00:33:27,890
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, the mind would be inconceivable

421
00:33:28,719 --> 00:33:33,241
[SPEAKER_01]: Without the natural manifestation upon which it stands, without name and form.

422
00:33:34,961 --> 00:33:41,524
[SPEAKER_01]: Without that body, that form, and that mental capacity in regard to it, your mind would not be there.

423
00:33:42,944 --> 00:33:48,546
[SPEAKER_01]: So, then you recognize that that body and the mental capacity in regard to it, the consciousness, that's not yours.

424
00:33:48,847 --> 00:33:53,608
[SPEAKER_01]: Because it's discovered through that determination that is the determination of your mind.

425
00:33:56,389 --> 00:33:57,850
[SPEAKER_01]: Which means the domain of those things,

426
00:33:58,442 --> 00:34:00,582
[SPEAKER_01]: are inaccessible to you, the domain of nāmarūpa.

427
00:34:02,943 --> 00:34:05,523
[SPEAKER_01]: The domain of pāsa is inaccessible to you.

428
00:34:09,284 --> 00:34:11,524
[SPEAKER_01]: Hence, you cannot, no, experience the pressure.

429
00:34:12,044 --> 00:34:14,825
[SPEAKER_01]: All you can do is surmount it internally.

430
00:34:20,546 --> 00:34:24,767
[SPEAKER_01]: And the fourth one is the origination of attention, that is the origination of phenomena.

431
00:34:25,447 --> 00:34:26,907
[SPEAKER_01]: What's the even subtler thing than your mind?

432
00:34:28,045 --> 00:34:35,409
[SPEAKER_01]: The particular movements of your mind, the little jumps, the little sort of hooks, the directions, that's what attention is.

433
00:34:36,429 --> 00:34:39,871
[SPEAKER_01]: But again, what does the attention depend on?

434
00:34:41,231 --> 00:34:51,296
[SPEAKER_01]: Just the... Well, actually, so, what I said for the third, it's actually more accurately said for the fourth, the nature of manifestation.

435
00:34:52,777 --> 00:34:54,238
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you can take nāmarūpa,

436
00:34:54,917 --> 00:34:56,998
[SPEAKER_01]: What does nāmarūpa has as its nature?

437
00:34:57,138 --> 00:34:58,279
[SPEAKER_01]: It's to manifest itself.

438
00:34:59,139 --> 00:35:01,920
[SPEAKER_01]: So, if you take the nature of manifestation, what does correspond to it?

439
00:35:02,861 --> 00:35:03,341
[SPEAKER_01]: Attention.

440
00:35:04,301 --> 00:35:05,982
[SPEAKER_01]: Because of that, you can jump at it.

441
00:35:06,102 --> 00:35:11,705
[SPEAKER_01]: Because of that, you can direct towards it.

442
00:35:11,725 --> 00:35:22,690
[SPEAKER_01]: So, when there is attending to something, when the attention is present, then what you have, through what you can discern through that attention is

443
00:35:23,776 --> 00:35:25,337
[SPEAKER_01]: The thing has a reason, i.e.

444
00:35:25,377 --> 00:35:36,422
[SPEAKER_01]: the arising is in you, the manifestation is there, of whatever, material or mental, doesn't matter.

445
00:35:38,423 --> 00:35:43,246
[SPEAKER_01]: So, if you can attend it, it's because it was given beforehand as an option to be attended to.

446
00:35:47,748 --> 00:35:49,809
[SPEAKER_01]: You could not possibly move your attention

447
00:35:50,998 --> 00:35:55,260
[SPEAKER_01]: But then you recognize, so me, moving my attention, it's completely secondary.

448
00:35:56,121 --> 00:36:01,243
[SPEAKER_01]: That's only possible because this thing has arisen beforehand, because of which I'm attending to it right now.

449
00:36:03,165 --> 00:36:05,246
[SPEAKER_01]: And that arising is something you're not saying.

450
00:36:06,206 --> 00:36:14,430
[SPEAKER_01]: Thus, your attention, then, cannot be yours, because your attention cannot not depend on this random arising of things.

451
00:36:14,911 --> 00:36:15,831
[SPEAKER_01]: It's just inconceivable.

452
00:36:16,111 --> 00:36:17,072
[SPEAKER_01]: What is there to attend then?

453
00:36:17,972 --> 00:36:19,113
[SPEAKER_01]: How can you even think of attention?

454
00:36:22,438 --> 00:36:25,579
[SPEAKER_01]: But, again, you could just take the first one, the course one.

455
00:36:25,599 --> 00:36:26,320
[SPEAKER_01]: That's what the Buddha said.

456
00:36:26,600 --> 00:36:32,983
[SPEAKER_01]: Or, he just remains mindful of this body there, to the extent necessary for the final knowledge.

457
00:36:33,624 --> 00:36:38,707
[SPEAKER_01]: So, this is just for different, basically different capacities, different people would have.

458
00:36:39,447 --> 00:36:54,622
[SPEAKER_01]: For some people, pondering on the principle between attention and the manifestation that manifested through the attention, because of which attention is there in the first place, is quite a palpable thing to contemplate on, to keep in their mind.

459
00:36:55,523 --> 00:36:56,804
[SPEAKER_01]: But for some people, it wouldn't be.

460
00:36:57,785 --> 00:37:03,591
[SPEAKER_01]: So that's why he kind of laid out the principle in all like four gradually

461
00:37:04,503 --> 00:37:09,725
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, increasing in subtlety, sort of, descriptions of the same principle.

462
00:37:10,485 --> 00:37:10,646
[SPEAKER_01]: Why?

463
00:37:10,706 --> 00:37:26,612
[SPEAKER_01]: Because if he only done it in terms of the body, then those people who were able to think in more subtle terms would see... well, mind you, they would figure it out themselves that it's the same principle, but the Buddha being, the Buddha Gautama being the one who's foremost in teaching the dhamma, would have expounded in every possible subtle way.

464
00:37:27,472 --> 00:37:28,633
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, actually,

465
00:37:29,245 --> 00:37:49,447
[SPEAKER_01]: Now, it comes to my mind, that other sutta in Digha Nikāya, the Buddha Vipassi, previous Buddha, the Buddha gives a story of him, whereby he, as a bodhisattva, discerned the principle of paticca-upāda, before he became a Buddha, and then, and then he starts describing it, vijjapācchā-saṅkāra, and so on, and then he comes to nāmarūpa determines the viññāṇa,

466
00:37:50,504 --> 00:37:52,526
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, viññāṇa determines another rūpa.

467
00:37:53,126 --> 00:37:54,828
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's where his pratītyapāda ended.

468
00:37:55,508 --> 00:37:58,211
[SPEAKER_01]: He did not take it further into avijjā and everything else.

469
00:37:58,251 --> 00:38:12,083
[SPEAKER_01]: And says, but when he kind of finished sort of clarifying that formulation, then he remained mindful of the rising and falling of the manifestation of the five aggregates, of the experience as a whole, for for a period of time until his mind was fully

470
00:38:15,173 --> 00:38:25,177
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you could see that that Samasambuddha was not as detailed, as prolific as the Buddha in terms of defining the principle to all its possible subtleties.

471
00:38:26,618 --> 00:38:27,338
[SPEAKER_01]: But the Buddha was.

472
00:38:28,298 --> 00:38:29,459
[SPEAKER_01]: But it's still the same principle.

473
00:38:31,500 --> 00:38:38,823
[SPEAKER_01]: So, in other words, I'm saying, take up just the first paragraph that you read, and perfect that principle, develop it,

474
00:38:39,765 --> 00:38:53,397
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, take it as far as you can, and it will result in your attention being freed from assumption in regard to manifestation.

